
  <sn><md>### Infinity Hosting

Sync a Local GitHub Repository to InfinityFree FTP (Without .git or .gitignore)

You keep your website in a GitHub repository, but your host is InfinityFree, which gives you FTP rather than Git deployment. Every update means dragging files into an FTP client and hoping you didn't forget one, or worse, accidentally uploading your `.git` folder and `.gitignore` file to a public web server.

This article shows several reliable ways to keep a local repository in sync with your InfinityFree account, with `.git/` and `.gitignore` always excluded. Pick the method that fits your workflow: a GUI client, a one-line command, or a fully automated GitHub Actions deploy.


